<section class="row row-even expanded-row">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="center-column">
      <p>
        <strong>Free</strong> and <strong>open source</strong>
        issue and task managment
        web application with a
        <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/" target="_blank">Ruby on Rails</a> backend.
        Along with
        <a href="https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/ERB.html" target="_blank">ERB</a>, it
        uses <a href="https://sass-lang.com/" target="_blank">SCSS</a> compiled to CSS and
        vanilla
        <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript" target="_blank">JavaScript</a>.
        In addition, it uses
        <a href="https://turbo.hotwired.dev/" target="_blank">Turbo</a> to make HTTP
        requests quicker.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="large-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("fork-repo") %>
        </div>
        <p>Source Code</p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://production.task-roller.net" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("globe") %>
        </div>
        <p>App in Action</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row row-odd">
  <div class="page">
    <h2>Feature Highlights</h2>

    <div class="feature-highlights-wrapper">
      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("code") %> Open Source</dt>
        <dd>
          Code is available on
          <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
          Bug reports and feature requests are welcome.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("options") %> Customizable Type Tags</dt>
        <dd>
          Editible names and options to provide control of organization.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("person-group") %> User Levels</dt>
        <dd>
          Four levels of user authorization allows separation of duties.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("fork-repo") %> GitHub Integrations</dt>
        <dd>
          Repo connection to support automatic import of issues and commit message
          callouts to progress App tasks.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("quote") %> Markdown Editors</dt>
        <dd>
          Text entry allows users to utilize HTML tags while being easy and intuitive.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <dl>
        <dt><%= icon("ribbon") %> Secure and Fully Tested</dt>
        <dd>
          Uses popular Ruby gems for auth, has a full suite of backend specs, and used in
          utilizes dogfooding.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <p class="center-text">
      <a href="/features" class="button no-margin">View Features</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row row-even">
  <h2>Deployment</h2>

  <div class="center-column">
    <p>
      The App can be deployed to your own server or to an application platform (PaaS) like
      <a href="https://www.heroku.com/" target="_blank">Heroku</a>. More over, there is a
      <a href="https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/" target="_blank">Dockerfile</a>
      available to make deployment more agnostic. Instructions on how to deploy
      and initially set up your instance are on
      <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">GitHub</a> with
      the source code.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
